# Build ignore rules for docker/Dockerfile.
# BuildKit picks this file up because it sits next to the Dockerfile with the
# name "<dockerfile>.dockerignore"; it takes precedence over a root
# .dockerignore, which BuildKit would then ignore — so keep only this one.
# Legacy (non-BuildKit) builders only read a root .dockerignore; with them the
# rules below are skipped, which is safe because the Dockerfile COPYs only
# explicitly listed files. Patterns are relative to the build context, i.e.
# the repository root:
#   docker build -t retentacle -f docker/Dockerfile .
# Exclude everything the image build does not need. The package itself and
# its packaging inputs (see Dockerfile) are copied explicitly.
.git
.github
.idea
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
temp/
tests/
data/

# Local files that must never end up in an image.
.DS_Store
configuration.yaml
retentacle_backups.json
retentacle_settings.json
retentacle_users.json
PLAN.md
CHANGELOG.md
docker/docker-compose.yml
docker/Dockerfile
docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore
